# Files the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` must not put in the Lambda image. The image needs the runtime
# modules (lambda.py, referenced_files.py, common/) and requirements.txt, which the Dockerfile copies
# on its own. CDK also hashes the build context through this file, so a change to a test no longer
# rebuilds the image. Docker still reads the Dockerfile and this file for the build; listing them only
# keeps them out of the copy.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
poetry.lock
pyproject.toml
.venv/
venv/
*.log
